            "\\subsection{Object-aware Prefix Tuning}\n",
            "To efficiently fine-tune the visual backbone, we present the Object-aware Prefix Tuning method that explicitly guides the visual understanding using objects (i.e., visual entities) as the learnable prefix. \n",
            "As shown in the bottom of Fig.~\\ref{fig2}, we utilize the CLIP model with $N$ Transformer layers as our visual backbone, and we feed two groups of features, $\\bm X_P$ and $\\bm X_I$, into CLIP using a prefix tuning approach as Eq.~\\ref{eq3}.\n",
            "Here, $\\bm X_P$ denotes the learnable prefix prompts, which are mixed with fine-grained visual object information, while $\\bm X_I$ represents the embeddings of each visual token encoded by the patch embedding layer. \n",
            "To mitigate catastrophic forgetting of the visual backbone, \n",
            "we freeze the parameters $\\bm \\Theta_v$ of the visual backbone and only make the prefix prompts $\\bm X_P$ learnable.\n",
            "\\begin{equation}\n",
